# ── Rust / Cargo ──────────────────────────────────────────────
/target/
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
# Cargo.lock IS committed (this is an application → reproducible builds)

# ── Journal databases & SQLite sidecars (never commit user data) ─
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
# EXCEPTION (after *.db — last match wins): the frozen, append-only test corpus IS committed.
# It is the CI gate against silent schema drift (story 1.10); see persistence/tests/corpus/README.md.
!persistence/tests/corpus/*.db

# ── Secrets / local config (keys live in the OS keychain, never here) ─
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
secrets/
config.local.*

# ── App-local config / backups / exports (runtime, not source) ───
/backups/
/exports/

# ── OS / editor noise ────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# ── Build / report output ────────────────────────────────────────
/dist/
*.log

# ── _bmad-output artifacts ──
# Legacy OLD-PROJECT artifacts (web/Leptos/Loco stack, Feb–May 2026) were DELETED 2026-06-09.
# _bmad-output/ now holds only current artifacts and is tracked normally (no allowlist needed).
# If Synology Drive re-syncs any legacy files back, delete them at the Synology source — do not commit.

# ── Tooling runtime noise (story-automator skill) ────────────────
__pycache__/
.claude/.story-automator-active
